only_use_override_person_properties unauthenticated on public /flags endpoint
only_use_override_person_properties is a new query parameter added to FlagsQueryParams and passed directly to evaluate_for_request without an is_internal_request check, unlike the parallel parameters detailed_analysis and override_flags_definitions which are both gated. Any caller with just a project token (the public SDK token) can send POST /flags?only_use_override_person_properties=true with an empty or attacker-controlled person_properties payload. This causes the evaluator to skip fetching person properties from the database entirely (PersonPropertyState::Skipped), so every DB-stored property value is treated as unset. A flag condition like plan = enterprise fails (bypass for "is set"/"equals" gates), while conditions like plan IS NOT SET or plan NOT EQUALS blocked spuriously match. Feature flags used as soft access gates on person-property conditions are bypassable by any SDK user. The intended use of this flag is for the internal Python test_evaluation flow which passes the INTERNAL_REQUEST_TOKEN; there is no reason for it to be available to unauthenticated public callers.

Prompt To Fix With AI
Gate `only_use_override_person_properties` behind `is_internal_request` in the same way `detailed_analysis` is gated, so external SDK callers cannot use it:

```rust
if context.meta.only_use_override_person_properties.unwrap_or(false)
    && authentication::is_internal_request(&context)
{
    Some(true)
} else {
    Some(false)
},
```

This matches the existing pattern used for `detailed_analysis` immediately above it.


